        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most 200-amp houses with two air conditioners, the Generac 7328 is the default 26kW pick: 24kW on natural gas, a service-rated switch and surge protection in the box, and the largest service network. The Kohler 26RCAL is the better-built alternative with the lowest full-load gas figure, and the Briggs & Stratton 040806 has the strongest motor-starting rating and a 7-year warranty.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Before buying any of them, get a load calculation, compare the natural gas rating rather than the label, and price load management against the size step. Many houses quoted 26kW are better served by a 24kW unit with two load managers, and the money saved pays for the gas meter and pipe work that decide whether the generator performs when it counts.
          </p>
